{
	"name": "Cunning Strikes",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/skills/wounds/injury-face-impact-orange.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 7th level, your scoundrel’s backstabbing shifts, allowing them to impose penalties upon their targets. When your scoundrel @UUID[Compendium.a5e-martial-artistry.class-features.Item.wwx7OmEQe7wLWmEz]{Backstabs}, they may choose one of the following options:</p><p><strong>Blind.</strong> Reduce the backstab damage by 2d4 to force the target to make a Constitution save. On a failed save, they become [[/condition id=blinded label=\"blind\"]] for a number of rounds equal to your proficiency bonus, or until an action is spent clearing the blood and/or detritus from their eyes.</p><p><strong>Hamstring.</strong> Reduce the backstab damage by 1d4 to reduce the target’s movement speed by 10ft for 1d4 rounds.</p><p><strong>Knockout.</strong> The attack deals only basic melee damage but the target must make a Constitution save or be knocked [[/condition id=unconscious]] for 1 round.</p>",
